1
00:05:23,076 --> 00:05:29,076
The universe is so much bigger than you realize.

2
00:10:46,153 --> 00:10:52,153
Everything Everywhere All at Once is a action, adventure,
science fiction film directed by Daniel Scheinert.

3
00:16:09,230 --> 00:16:15,230
An aging Chinese immigrant is swept up in an insane adventure, where she alone can save what's
important to her by connecting with the lives she could have led in other universes.

4
00:21:32,307 --> 00:21:38,307
Evelyn Wang, played by Michelle Yeoh.

5
00:26:55,384 --> 00:27:01,384
Joy Wang / Jobu Tupaki, played by Stephanie Hsu.

6
00:32:18,461 --> 00:32:24,461
Waymond Wang, played by Ke Huy Quan.

7
00:37:41,538 --> 00:37:47,538
Gong Gong, played by James Hong.

8
00:43:04,615 --> 00:43:10,615
Deirdre Beaubeirdre, played by Jamie Lee Curtis.

9
00:48:27,692 --> 00:48:33,692
Becky Sregor, played by Tallie Medel.

10
00:53:50,769 --> 00:53:56,769
Everything Everywhere All at Once is a 2022 American independent absurdist comedy-drama film written and directed
by Daniel Kwan and Daniel Scheinert, who produced it with Anthony and Joe Russo and Jonathan Wang.

11
00:59:13,846 --> 00:59:19,846
The film incorporates media from several genres and film mediums, including surreal comedy,
science fiction, fantasy, martial arts films, immigrant narrative, and animation.

12
01:04:36,923 --> 01:04:42,923
Michelle Yeoh stars as Evelyn Quan Wang, a Chinese-American immigrant who, while being audited by the IRS, discovers that she
must connect with parallel universe versions of herself to prevent a powerful being from destroying the multiverse.

13
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
The film also stars Stephanie Hsu, Ke Huy Quan,
James Hong, and Jamie Lee Curtis.

14
01:15:23,076 --> 01:15:29,076
Kwan and Scheinert began work on the project in 2010.

15
01:20:46,153 --> 01:20:52,153
Production was announced in 2018, and principal
photography ran from January to March 2020.

16
01:26:09,230 --> 01:26:15,230
The works of Hong Kong film director Wong Kar-wai, as well as the children's book Sylvester and the
Magic Pebble and the video game Everything, served as inspiration for several scenes.

17
01:31:32,307 --> 01:31:38,307
Also inspired by contemporary scholars such as philosopher Mary-Jane Rubenstein, the film explores philosophical themes such as existentialism,
nihilism, surrealism, and absurdism, as well as themes such as neurodivergence, depression, generational trauma, and Asian American identity.

18
01:36:55,384 --> 01:37:01,384
Its soundtrack features compositions by Son Lux, and collaborations with
Mitski, David Byrne, André 3000, John Hampson, and Randy Newman.

19
01:42:18,461 --> 01:42:24,461
Everything Everywhere All at Once premiered at South by Southwest on March 11, 2022, and began a limited
theatrical release in the United States on March 25, before a wide release by A24 on April 8.

20
01:47:41,538 --> 01:47:47,538
Grossing $143 million against a $14–25 million budget,
it became A24's highest-grossing film.

21
01:53:04,615 --> 01:53:10,615
The film garnered widespread acclaim from critics
and received numerous accolades.

22
01:58:27,692 --> 01:58:33,692
At the 95th Academy Awards, it won seven out of the eleven awards it was nominated for: Best Picture, Best Actress (Yeoh), Best Supporting Actor
(Quan), Best Supporting Actress (Curtis), Best Director and Best Original Screenplay for Kwan and Scheinert, and Best Editing.

23
02:03:50,769 --> 02:03:56,769
The film also won two Golden Globe Awards, five Critics' Choice Awards (including Best
Picture), a BAFTA Award, and a record four SAG Awards, including Best Ensemble.

24
02:09:13,846 --> 02:09:19,846
The film explores themes of mother, martial arts, kung fu, nihilism, philosophy.

25
02:14:36,923 --> 02:14:42,923
The tone is thought_provoking and mind_bending.
